  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44245874",
      "title": "Managing Form-dependent State with useActionState()",
      "sourceHash": "58697f2f1f5d963d864c7c09e6143efbc7d61a741210642f57bd71f7f668765b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "So how can we now use this errors array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 9.51,
          "en": "to show error messages to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.51,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "when they submit an invalid form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 16.143,
          "en": "when using this React form action's feature?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "Well, in this action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 25.74,
          "en": "we could check if our errors array has a length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.74,
          "end": 27.54,
          "en": "that is greater than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.54,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "So if we have at least one error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 32.1,
          "en": "And if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.1,
          "end": 35.22,
          "en": "we could return an object, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 39.66,
          "en": "though you can return anything in such a action function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "You don't have to return anything at all actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 45.39,
          "en": "but if you do want to return something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "it can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "And here it's an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 53.25,
          "en": "an object where I'll set the errors key, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.25,
          "end": 55.14,
          "en": "to my errors array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.14,
          "end": 57.81,
          "en": "But that key name is totally up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.81,
          "end": 59.49,
          "en": "because you can, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "return any value of your choice, or nothing at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "And therefore, if you return an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "the shape of that object is also totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 74.1,
          "en": "But here I wanna return an object that has an errors key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 77.03999999999999,
          "en": "and the value for that errors key is my errors array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.03999999999999,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "And since I have the same names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "I can use this JavaScript shortcut to create this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "with this key value pair like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.93,
          "en": "Now, if we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "so if we have no errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "I therefore wanna return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "where errors is set to null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 98.61,
          "en": "so that I have some indicator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.61,
          "end": 100.71000000000001,
          "en": "whether we have errors or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.71000000000001,
          "end": 102.6,
          "en": "If it's null, we have no errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "If it's an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 106.38300000000001,
          "en": "we have errors at least one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "But how can we use this return value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "when using this form action's feature?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 115.56,
          "en": "Because this action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.56,
          "end": 119.55,
          "en": "is passed as a value to this action prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.55,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "how do we now get hold of that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 125.43299999999999,
          "en": "that's returned by that action function?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 127.59,
          "en": "Well, for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "React gives us a special hook that we can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 136.77,
          "en": "a special hook that must be imported from React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.77,
          "end": 138.97,
          "en": "a special hook that's called useActionState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 145.07999999999998,
          "en": "And that's a new hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.07999999999998,
          "end": 148.14,
          "en": "that was added with React version 19.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "So if you're using an older version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 151.56,
          "en": "you can't use this hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "but that shouldn't be a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 156,
          "en": "because you also can't set a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 158.28300000000002,
          "en": "as a value for the action prop there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.54,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "So I have this useActionState hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 164.703,
          "en": "how do we now use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 167.25,
          "en": "Well, like all hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.25,
          "end": 169.77,
          "en": "you must use it in your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 171.45,
          "en": "or inside of some other hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.45,
          "end": 176.07,
          "en": "And here I'll use it after this signupAction function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 179.853,
          "en": "which I collapsed here so that it takes up less space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.69,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "So useActionState is called here after this action function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 187.53,
          "en": "and I'm calling it after this action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.53,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "because this action function now actually must be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 196.893,
          "en": "as a first argument to this useActionState hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.82,
          "end": 199.89,
          "en": "So this useActionState hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.89,
          "end": 204.483,
          "en": "wants a action function as a first input value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 209.19,
          "en": "but that's not all useActionState wants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.19,
          "end": 211.71,
          "en": "Instead, as its name implies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.71,
          "end": 216.71,
          "en": "this hook aims to manage some form-related state for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.65,
          "end": 220.14,
          "en": "or some action-related state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 223.26,
          "en": "But actions of course are related to forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.26,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "so in the end, it's some form-related state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 228.12,
          "en": "that's being managed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.12,
          "end": 231.42000000000002,
          "en": "And therefore this useActionState hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.42000000000002,
          "end": 234.72,
          "en": "actually also wants a second value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.72,
          "end": 238.68,
          "en": "where you provide an initial state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.68,
          "end": 240.6,
          "en": "Because this action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.6,
          "end": 244.11,
          "en": "may then return an updated state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.11,
          "end": 246.633,
          "en": "this object which we return here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.53,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "but if the form has never been submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 253.98,
          "en": "of course this action function will have never executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 253.98,
          "end": 256.74,
          "en": "and therefore no value will have been returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.74,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "at any point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 261.69,
          "en": "That's why you also must provide an initial state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 261.69,
          "end": 262.68,
          "en": "for this hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.68,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "which will be active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 267.51,
          "en": "if the action has not been executed yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.51,
          "end": 270.24,
          "en": "And in my case, that is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.24,
          "end": 273.03,
          "en": "where I'll set the errors key to null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.03,
          "end": 276.09000000000003,
          "en": "because initially if the form hasn't been submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.09000000000003,
          "end": 279.63,
          "en": "I don't want to show any errors to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 279.63,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "because they didn't even have a chance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 284.433,
          "en": "of inserting any values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.3,
          "end": 288.39,
          "en": "So that's the initial state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 288.39,
          "end": 292.98,
          "en": "Now, useActionState does not just take input values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 292.98,
          "end": 296.15999999999997,
          "en": "but it also returns something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 296.15999999999997,
          "end": 299.31,
          "en": "and it does return an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.31,
          "end": 302.88,
          "en": "and therefore we can use array destructuring here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.88,
          "end": 306,
          "en": "to store the different array elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 306,
          "end": 309.78,
          "en": "in different variables or constants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.78,
          "end": 312.27,
          "en": "So just like the useState hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 312.27,
          "end": 313.74,
          "en": "which you already know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.74,
          "end": 316.69,
          "en": "useActionState also returns an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 317.58,
          "end": 321.453,
          "en": "and it does return an array with three elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 325.71,
          "en": "And the first element it returns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.71,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "is the current formState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 331.14300000000003,
          "en": "So initially, this initial state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.1,
          "end": 335.07,
          "en": "But then once the action has been executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.07,
          "end": 338.163,
          "en": "the state that was returned by that action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.3,
          "end": 341.97,
          "en": "So those return values here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.97,
          "end": 344.19,
          "en": "that's then what will be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.19,
          "end": 347.613,
          "en": "in this formState constant or variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.6,
          "end": 353.58,
          "en": "And that's how we can get access to these return values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.58,
          "end": 356.88,
          "en": "because formState will eventually contain them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "But that's not the only thing we get in this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 362.73,
          "en": "that's returned by useActionState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 362.73,
          "end": 365.91,
          "en": "Instead as a second element in that array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 365.91,
          "end": 369.27,
          "en": "we get an updated formAction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 369.27,
          "end": 372.54,
          "en": "Now we pass an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 372.54,
          "end": 375.54,
          "en": "as a first argument to useActionState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 375.54,
          "end": 380.54,
          "en": "and internally React then kind of creates a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 384.423,
          "en": "that's wrapped around our action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 387.87,
          "en": "And it does that so that it can listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 387.87,
          "end": 392.19,
          "en": "to the invocation of this action, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 392.19,
          "end": 396.06,
          "en": "That's why we get back and updated formAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 396.06,
          "end": 398.79,
          "en": "which in the end is our formAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 398.79,
          "end": 401.673,
          "en": "but enhanced by React, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 402.69,
          "end": 404.94,
          "en": "So this formAction which we get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.94,
          "end": 408.54,
          "en": "is our formAction with extra features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 408.54,
          "end": 410.94,
          "en": "or with React being aware of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 410.94,
          "end": 413.1,
          "en": "if you want to call it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 413.1,
          "end": 413.94,
          "en": "And it's there for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 413.94,
          "end": 417.54,
          "en": "This formAction which we get back from useActionState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.54,
          "end": 422.073,
          "en": "which should be set as a value for this action prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 422.91,
          "end": 427.91,
          "en": "So this action is set as a value here for the action prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 429.24,
          "end": 431.73,
          "en": "Well, and the last element we get back here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 431.73,
          "end": 435.54,
          "en": "is a pending element, which is true or false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 435.54,
          "end": 438.27,
          "en": "depending on whether the form is currently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 438.27,
          "end": 440.52,
          "en": "being submitted or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 440.52,
          "end": 442.89,
          "en": "Now in this case, this doesn't make much sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 442.89,
          "end": 447.51,
          "en": "because this action executes pretty much instantly anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 447.51,
          "end": 450,
          "en": "so it won't be pending for long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 450,
          "end": 454.26,
          "en": "But later in this section when we explore async actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 454.26,
          "end": 455.22,
          "en": "that will change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 455.22,
          "end": 458.283,
          "en": "But for the moment, I don't need that pending value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 459.12,
          "end": 461.79,
          "en": "But I do want to work with that formState now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 461.79,
          "end": 462.9,
          "en": "because as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 462.9,
          "end": 466.56,
          "en": "eventually it may contain the error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 466.56,
          "end": 471.56,
          "en": "which we pass back here if we have errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 471.57,
          "end": 474.33,
          "en": "And therefore we can use it here in our form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 474.33,
          "end": 478.173,
          "en": "maybe at the bottom of that form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 479.52,
          "end": 482.91,
          "en": "let's say right above these buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 482.91,
          "end": 487.68,
          "en": "to conditionally output some error messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 487.68,
          "end": 492.68,
          "en": "So here I'll check if formState.errors is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 492.96,
          "end": 494.73,
          "en": "so if it's not null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 494.73,
          "end": 497.26,
          "en": "which it is initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 498.39,
          "end": 501.513,
          "en": "and which it is if no errors were found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 502.44,
          "end": 503.55,
          "en": "But if it's not null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 503.55,
          "end": 506.073,
          "en": "so if it contains this errors array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 507.06,
          "end": 511.35,
          "en": "then I wanna output something down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 511.35,
          "end": 514.29,
          "en": "I wanna output an unordered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 514.29,
          "end": 519.29,
          "en": "with a class name of errors for styling purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 520.47,
          "end": 523.14,
          "en": "And in that unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 523.14,
          "end": 525.21,
          "en": "I'll go through my errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 525.21,
          "end": 528.54,
          "en": "and map every error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 528.54,
          "end": 530.77,
          "en": "to a list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 531.84,
          "end": 535.65,
          "en": "where the key can be the error message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 535.65,
          "end": 539.313,
          "en": "and where I then also wanna output that error or message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 541.08,
          "end": 542.43,
          "en": "And that should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 542.43,
          "end": 545.733,
          "en": "that error messages are displayed if we got some.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 547.35,
          "end": 549.36,
          "en": "Now with that, if we save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 549.36,
          "end": 551.49,
          "en": "if we go back to our form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 551.49,
          "end": 554.91,
          "en": "and I click sign up without entering anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 554.91,
          "end": 558.963,
          "en": "I get an error that formData.get is not a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 560.58,
          "end": 562.41,
          "en": "And I get this error now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 562.41,
          "end": 566.37,
          "en": "because when using this useActionState hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 566.37,
          "end": 568.92,
          "en": "this formAction function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 568.92,
          "end": 571.38,
          "en": "which we pass to useActionState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 571.38,
          "end": 574.77,
          "en": "so this signupAction function in our case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 574.77,
          "end": 578.523,
          "en": "is called in a different way than it was called before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 579.45,
          "end": 582.51,
          "en": "Previously without using useActionState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 582.51,
          "end": 586.56,
          "en": "our action function was called and the formData was passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 586.56,
          "end": 590.07,
          "en": "as the first and only input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 590.07,
          "end": 594.27,
          "en": "to this action function by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 594.27,
          "end": 596.87,
          "en": "But when passing signupAction to the useActionState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 598.65,
          "end": 601.38,
          "en": "this action function will be called differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 601.38,
          "end": 605.01,
          "en": "And formData will actually be the second input value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 605.01,
          "end": 607.47,
          "en": "the second parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 607.47,
          "end": 612.03,
          "en": "because the first parameter will be the previous form state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 612.03,
          "end": 614.76,
          "en": "so the old form state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 614.76,
          "end": 616.92,
          "en": "because of course it's possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 616.92,
          "end": 619.71,
          "en": "that this action is invoked multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 619.71,
          "end": 620.85,
          "en": "And in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 620.85,
          "end": 625.08,
          "en": "React gives you the last form state it was aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 625.08,
          "end": 626.85,
          "en": "as an input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 626.85,
          "end": 631.85,
          "en": "in case you wanted to base your new state on that old state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 632.85,
          "end": 635.73,
          "en": "And the first time this is being executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 635.73,
          "end": 640.32,
          "en": "the previous form state will simply be that initial state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 640.32,
          "end": 641.943,
          "en": "that's being passed to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 643.35,
          "end": 647.76,
          "en": "Now here, I don't really need that previous form state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 647.76,
          "end": 651.06,
          "en": "but nonetheless we need to accept it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 651.06,
          "end": 654.06,
          "en": "and extract formData as a second parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 654.06,
          "end": 656.493,
          "en": "since we'll get an error otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 657.36,
          "end": 660.3,
          "en": "But with that done, if we now save this and go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 660.3,
          "end": 662.28,
          "en": "if I now click sign up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 662.28,
          "end": 665.883,
          "en": "you see now I get these errors down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 667.29,
          "end": 669.21,
          "en": "And the styling is a bit off",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 669.21,
          "end": 671.04,
          "en": "because in my form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 671.04,
          "end": 673.98,
          "en": "the class here should be error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 673.98,
          "end": 675.543,
          "en": "not errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 676.77,
          "end": 678.24,
          "en": "But with that done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 678.24,
          "end": 680.253,
          "en": "this now looks better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 681.3,
          "end": 683.13,
          "en": "So that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 683.13,
          "end": 685.65,
          "en": "But we currently have a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 685.65,
          "end": 690.65,
          "en": "If I enter a valid email address, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 690.69,
          "end": 693,
          "en": "and I then click sign up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 693,
          "end": 695.49,
          "en": "the overall form of course is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 695.49,
          "end": 697.26,
          "en": "And that's why I'm getting some errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 697.26,
          "end": 700.32,
          "en": "though I'm not getting the email error message anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 700.32,
          "end": 703.47,
          "en": "because that was a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 703.47,
          "end": 704.97,
          "en": "But as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 704.97,
          "end": 707.85,
          "en": "the field here was cleared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 707.85,
          "end": 711.12,
          "en": "because every time you submit a form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 711.12,
          "end": 714.93,
          "en": "when using this React form action's feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 714.93,
          "end": 719.52,
          "en": "React resets the form for you in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 719.52,
          "end": 722.43,
          "en": "And that's of course not what I want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 722.43,
          "end": 724.86,
          "en": "If I have some invalid values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 724.86,
          "end": 728.49,
          "en": "I definitely don't wanna throw the valid values away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 728.49,
          "end": 730.59,
          "en": "Or in general, I don't want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 730.59,
          "end": 733.11,
          "en": "throw the values the user entered away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 733.11,
          "end": 735.783,
          "en": "That's not a good user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 736.74,
          "end": 739.803,
          "en": "So that's the next thing we'll have to fix here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
